# Wave W17-AC (Route 227): flow post — a cooled-flow marker post at the ash field’s edge: a weathered post carrying one slanted shard of cooled glass at its head, teal-dark with a single pale edge — the design’s glass ribbons standing in the prop register (design: cooled flows trail glass ribbons off the mountain; the ribbons themselves are dressing over byte-preserved cells — the posts mark where you do not step). On stark turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from the fleet’s marker posts by the shard entire: posts mark a road, this one marks a flow.
